window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b361-786e897b2d77509d.json"]={sha256:"786e897b2d77509dce6052456a1fe464e1ecd1433504e462afd0f76b4aba154a",value:{"id":"b361","title":"高速鐵路受流性能驗證","titleEn":"Current-collection verification for high-speed rail","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"高速鐵路受流性能驗證以「接觸力離線受流率與測試不確定度」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。受電弓與電車線耦合時，平均接觸力、力的散布、離線與電弧必須分開量測，單一平均值無法描述短暫中斷。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops contact force contact loss and test uncertainty through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Coupled pantograph and contact-line behavior requires separate measures of mean force, dispersion, loss of contact and arcing; a mean cannot describe brief interruptions. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-power","subcategoryTitle":"牽引供電與受流","subcategoryTitleEn":"Traction power and current collection","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-power","learningTags":["rail","rail-power","power"],"architectureFamily":"rail-power","architectureNodes":[["弓線接觸","Pantograph contact"],["力與加速度","Force and acceleration"],["離線電弧","Contact loss and arcs"],["同步量測","Synchronized sensing"],["不確定度","Uncertainty"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,2],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,2]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-power","labels":["弓線接觸","力與加速度","離線電弧","同步量測","不確定度"],"labelsEn":["Pantograph contact","Force and acceleration","Contact loss and arcs","Synchronized sensing","Uncertainty"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N；y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N。只把 F1 增加百分之十，y=113 N。模型邊界：等時距三筆合成取樣；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N；y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N。只把 F1 增加百分之十，y=103.512 N。模型邊界：等權有限樣本均方根；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N; y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N. Increasing only F1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=113 N. Boundary: Three equally spaced synthetic samples; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N. Increasing only F1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=103.512 N. Boundary: Equal-weight finite-sample RMS; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b361-v16-s1","title":"平均接觸力與接觸力均方根","titleEn":"Mean contact force & Contact-force RMS","description":"本階段聚焦「平均接觸力」與「接觸力均方根」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Mean contact force\" and \"Contact-force RMS\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b361-v16-01","title":"平均接觸力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mean contact force: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「平均接觸力」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mean contact force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平均力描述時窗中央趨勢而不保證持續接觸。本模型把 F1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 113 N。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。等時距三筆合成取樣。使用最小力與接觸影像作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；正常平均可同時含零接觸片段，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「平均接觸力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mean force describes the central tendency of a window without guaranteeing continuous contact. In this model, F1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 113 N. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Three equally spaced synthetic samples. Use minimum force and contact images as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mean contact force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N；y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N; y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「平均接觸力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mean contact force”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-01-k1","title":"平均接觸力","titleEn":"Mean contact force","text":"平均力描述時窗中央趨勢而不保證持續接觸。本模型把 F1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 113 N。","textEn":"Mean force describes the central tendency of a window without guaranteeing continuous contact. In this model, F1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「平均接觸力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mean contact force\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段","平均力描述時窗中央趨勢而不保證持續接觸。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals.","Mean force describes the central tendency of a window without guaranteeing continuous contact.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均力描述時窗中央趨勢而不保證持續接觸。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mean force describes the central tendency of a window without guaranteeing continuous contact. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b361-v16-02","title":"平均接觸力：定量估算","titleEn":"Mean contact force: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「平均接觸力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mean contact force” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N；y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N。只把 F1 增加百分之十，y=113 N。模型邊界：等時距三筆合成取樣；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N; y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N. Increasing only F1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=113 N. Boundary: Three equally spaced synthetic samples; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以最小力與接觸影像區分模型與觀察，先用低載力計與同步攝影建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use minimum force and contact images to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N；y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N。只把 F1 增加百分之十，y=113 N。模型邊界：等時距三筆合成取樣；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N; y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N. Increasing only F1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=113 N. Boundary: Three equally spaced synthetic samples; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「平均接觸力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mean contact force\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N；y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N; y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N；y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=90 N, F2=110 N, F3=130 N; y=(F1+F2+F3)/3=110 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b361-v16-03","title":"平均接觸力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mean contact force: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「平均接觸力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mean contact force” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以最小力與接觸影像區分模型與觀察，先用低載力計與同步攝影建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平均接觸力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use minimum force and contact images to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load force gauge and synchronized video, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Mean contact force. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「平均接觸力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出等時距三筆合成取樣如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由正常平均可同時含零接觸片段造成偏離的合成觀察，以最小力與接觸影像說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Mean contact force, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Three equally spaced synthetic samples. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals. Explain which evidence in minimum force and contact images distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以最小力與接觸影像區分模型與觀察，先用低載力計與同步攝影建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平均接觸力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use minimum force and contact images to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load force gauge and synchronized video, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Mean contact force. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「平均接觸力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出等時距三筆合成取樣如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由正常平均可同時含零接觸片段造成偏離的合成觀察，以最小力與接觸影像說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Mean contact force, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Three equally spaced synthetic samples. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals. Explain which evidence in minimum force and contact images distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「平均接觸力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mean contact force\"?","options":["本單元以最小力與接觸影像區分模型與觀察，先用低載力計與同步攝影建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動"],"optionsEn":["Use minimum force and contact images to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以最小力與接觸影像區分模型與觀察，先用低載力計與同步攝影建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use minimum force and contact images to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b361-v16-04","title":"平均接觸力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mean contact force: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「平均接觸力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mean contact force” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"正常平均可同時含零接觸片段。這個失效與「平均接觸力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查最小力與接觸影像，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals. This failure and a measurement bias in Mean contact force can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check minimum force and contact images rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用最小力與接觸影像作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；正常平均可同時含零接觸片段，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"正常平均可同時含零接觸片段。這個失效與「平均接觸力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查最小力與接觸影像，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals. This failure and a measurement bias in Mean contact force can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check minimum force and contact images rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「平均接觸力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mean contact force\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","正常平均可同時含零接觸片段。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"正常平均可同時含零接觸片段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b361-v16-05","title":"接觸力均方根：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Contact-force RMS: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「接觸力均方根」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Contact-force RMS” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均方根與算術平均反映不同的力統計。本模型把 F1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 103.512 N。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。等權有限樣本均方根。使用完整力時序與均值作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接觸力均方根」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"RMS and arithmetic mean describe different force statistics. In this model, F1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 103.512 N. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Equal-weight finite-sample RMS. Use complete force time history and mean as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Contact-force RMS” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N；y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接觸力均方根」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Contact-force RMS”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-05-k1","title":"接觸力均方根","titleEn":"Contact-force RMS","text":"均方根與算術平均反映不同的力統計。本模型把 F1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 103.512 N。","textEn":"RMS and arithmetic mean describe different force statistics. In this model, F1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸力均方根」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Contact-force RMS\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布","均方根與算術平均反映不同的力統計。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread.","RMS and arithmetic mean describe different force statistics."],"answer":2,"explanation":"均方根與算術平均反映不同的力統計。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"RMS and arithmetic mean describe different force statistics. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b361-v16-06","title":"接觸力均方根：定量估算","titleEn":"Contact-force RMS: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接觸力均方根」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Contact-force RMS” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N；y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N。只把 F1 增加百分之十，y=103.512 N。模型邊界：等權有限樣本均方根；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N. Increasing only F1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=103.512 N. Boundary: Equal-weight finite-sample RMS; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以完整力時序與均值區分模型與觀察，先用離線力資料與校正表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use complete force time history and mean to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N；y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N。只把 F1 增加百分之十，y=103.512 N。模型邊界：等權有限樣本均方根；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N. Increasing only F1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=103.512 N. Boundary: Equal-weight finite-sample RMS; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接觸力均方根」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Contact-force RMS\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: External flashes may create false arc detections.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N；y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt((F1**2+F2**2+F3**2)/3)=101.325 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b361-v16-07","title":"接觸力均方根：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Contact-force RMS: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接觸力均方根」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Contact-force RMS” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以完整力時序與均值區分模型與觀察，先用離線力資料與校正表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接觸力均方根」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use complete force time history and mean to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using offline force data and calibration sheet, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Contact-force RMS. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「接觸力均方根」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出等權有限樣本均方根如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋造成偏離的合成觀察，以完整力時序與均值說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Contact-force RMS, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Equal-weight finite-sample RMS. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them. Explain which evidence in complete force time history and mean distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以完整力時序與均值區分模型與觀察，先用離線力資料與校正表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接觸力均方根」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use complete force time history and mean to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using offline force data and calibration sheet, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Contact-force RMS. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「接觸力均方根」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出等權有限樣本均方根如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋造成偏離的合成觀察，以完整力時序與均值說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Contact-force RMS, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Equal-weight finite-sample RMS. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them. Explain which evidence in complete force time history and mean distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接觸力均方根」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Contact-force RMS\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以完整力時序與均值區分模型與觀察，先用離線力資料與校正表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use complete force time history and mean to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以完整力時序與均值區分模型與觀察，先用離線力資料與校正表建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use complete force time history and mean to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b361-v16-08","title":"接觸力均方根：失效診斷","titleEn":"Contact-force RMS: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接觸力均方根」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Contact-force RMS” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋。這個失效與「接觸力均方根」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查完整力時序與均值，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them. This failure and a measurement bias in Contact-force RMS can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check complete force time history and mean rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用完整力時序與均值作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋。這個失效與「接觸力均方根」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查完整力時序與均值，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them. This failure and a measurement bias in Contact-force RMS can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check complete force time history and mean rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接觸力均方根」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Contact-force RMS\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布","少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread.","A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them."],"answer":2,"explanation":"少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b361-v16-s2","title":"力散布標準差與離線時間比例","titleEn":"Contact-force population deviation & Loss-of-contact duration fraction","description":"本階段聚焦「力散布標準差」與「離線時間比例」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Contact-force population deviation\" and \"Loss-of-contact duration fraction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b361-v16-09","title":"力散布標準差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Contact-force population deviation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「力散布標準差」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Contact-force population deviation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"全體樣本標準差量化此時窗相對均值的散布。本模型把 F1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出減少為 13.1993 N。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。三個等權樣本的全體標準差，式內平均隨擾動重算。使用時窗分段後散布作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「力散布標準差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Population deviation quantifies spread about the mean in this window. In this model, F1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output decreases to 13.1993 N. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Population deviation of three equally weighted samples, with the mean recalculated inside the expression. Use spread in segmented windows as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Contact-force population deviation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N；y=sqrt(((F1-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F2-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F3-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2)/3)=16.3299 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt(((F1-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F2-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F3-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2)/3)=16.3299 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「力散布標準差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Contact-force population deviation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-09-k1","title":"力散布標準差","titleEn":"Contact-force population deviation","text":"全體樣本標準差量化此時窗相對均值的散布。本模型把 F1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出減少為 13.1993 N。","textEn":"Population deviation quantifies spread about the mean in this window. In this model, F1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「力散布標準差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Contact-force population deviation\" is correct?","options":["全體樣本標準差量化此時窗相對均值的散布。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間"],"optionsEn":["Population deviation quantifies spread about the mean in this window.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"全體樣本標準差量化此時窗相對均值的散布。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Population deviation quantifies spread about the mean in this window. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b361-v16-10","title":"力散布標準差：定量估算","titleEn":"Contact-force population deviation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「力散布標準差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Contact-force population deviation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N；y=sqrt(((F1-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F2-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F3-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2)/3)=16.3299 N。只把 F1 增加百分之十，y=13.1993 N。模型邊界：三個等權樣本的全體標準差，式內平均隨擾動重算；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt(((F1-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F2-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F3-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2)/3)=16.3299 N. Increasing only F1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=13.1993 N. Boundary: Population deviation of three equally weighted samples, with the mean recalculated inside the expression; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以時窗分段後散布區分模型與觀察，先用合成時序分段統計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use spread in segmented windows to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N；y=sqrt(((F1-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F2-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F3-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2)/3)=16.3299 N。只把 F1 增加百分之十，y=13.1993 N。模型邊界：三個等權樣本的全體標準差，式內平均隨擾動重算；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt(((F1-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F2-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F3-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2)/3)=16.3299 N. Increasing only F1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=13.1993 N. Boundary: Population deviation of three equally weighted samples, with the mean recalculated inside the expression; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「力散布標準差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Contact-force population deviation\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N；y=sqrt(((F1-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F2-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F3-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2)/3)=16.3299 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F1=80 N, F2=100 N, F3=120 N; y=sqrt(((F1-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F2-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2+(F3-(F1+F2+F3)/3)**2)/3)=16.3299 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b361-v16-11","title":"力散布標準差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Contact-force population deviation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「力散布標準差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Contact-force population deviation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以時窗分段後散布區分模型與觀察，先用合成時序分段統計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「力散布標準差」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use spread in segmented windows to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using segmented statistics of a synthetic trace, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Contact-force population deviation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「力散布標準差」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出三個等權樣本的全體標準差，式內平均隨擾動重算如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布造成偏離的合成觀察，以時窗分段後散布說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Contact-force population deviation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Population deviation of three equally weighted samples, with the mean recalculated inside the expression. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread. Explain which evidence in spread in segmented windows distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以時窗分段後散布區分模型與觀察，先用合成時序分段統計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「力散布標準差」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use spread in segmented windows to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using segmented statistics of a synthetic trace, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Contact-force population deviation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「力散布標準差」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出三個等權樣本的全體標準差，式內平均隨擾動重算如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布造成偏離的合成觀察，以時窗分段後散布說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Contact-force population deviation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Population deviation of three equally weighted samples, with the mean recalculated inside the expression. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread. Explain which evidence in spread in segmented windows distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「力散布標準差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Contact-force population deviation\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度","本單元以時窗分段後散布區分模型與觀察，先用合成時序分段統計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty.","Use spread in segmented windows to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以時窗分段後散布區分模型與觀察，先用合成時序分段統計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use spread in segmented windows to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b361-v16-12","title":"力散布標準差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Contact-force population deviation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「力散布標準差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Contact-force population deviation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布。這個失效與「力散布標準差」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查時窗分段後散布，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread. This failure and a measurement bias in Contact-force population deviation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check spread in segmented windows rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用時窗分段後散布作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布。這個失效與「力散布標準差」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查時窗分段後散布，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread. This failure and a measurement bias in Contact-force population deviation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check spread in segmented windows rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「力散布標準差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Contact-force population deviation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間"],"optionsEn":["Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b361-v16-13","title":"離線時間比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Loss-of-contact duration fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「離線時間比例」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Loss-of-contact duration fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"持續時間比與離線事件數是不同指標。本模型把 lost 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.44 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。固定辨識門檻的合成時窗。使用離線起迄時間與事件數作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「離線時間比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Duration fraction and number of contact-loss events are different metrics. In this model, lost is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.44 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Synthetic window with a fixed detection definition. Use contact-loss start/end times and event count as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Loss-of-contact duration fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=0.08 s, total=20 s；y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=0.08 s, total=20 s; y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「離線時間比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Loss-of-contact duration fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-13-k1","title":"離線時間比例","titleEn":"Loss-of-contact duration fraction","text":"持續時間比與離線事件數是不同指標。本模型把 lost 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.44 percent。","textEn":"Duration fraction and number of contact-loss events are different metrics. In this model, lost is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「離線時間比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Loss-of-contact duration fraction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間","持續時間比與離線事件數是不同指標。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations.","Duration fraction and number of contact-loss events are different metrics.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: External flashes may create false arc detections."],"answer":1,"explanation":"持續時間比與離線事件數是不同指標。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Duration fraction and number of contact-loss events are different metrics. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b361-v16-14","title":"離線時間比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Loss-of-contact duration fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「離線時間比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Loss-of-contact duration fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=0.08 s, total=20 s；y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent。只把 lost 增加百分之十，y=0.44 percent。模型邊界：固定辨識門檻的合成時窗；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=0.08 s, total=20 s; y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent. Increasing only lost with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.44 percent. Boundary: Synthetic window with a fixed detection definition; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以離線起迄時間與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用接觸狀態重播與共同時鐘建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use contact-loss start/end times and event count to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=0.08 s, total=20 s；y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent。只把 lost 增加百分之十，y=0.44 percent。模型邊界：固定辨識門檻的合成時窗；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=0.08 s, total=20 s; y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent. Increasing only lost with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.44 percent. Boundary: Synthetic window with a fixed detection definition; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「離線時間比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Loss-of-contact duration fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=0.08 s, total=20 s；y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=0.08 s, total=20 s; y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：lost=0.08 s, total=20 s；y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: lost=0.08 s, total=20 s; y=lost/total*100=0.4 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b361-v16-15","title":"離線時間比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Loss-of-contact duration fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「離線時間比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Loss-of-contact duration fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以離線起迄時間與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用接觸狀態重播與共同時鐘建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「離線時間比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use contact-loss start/end times and event count to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using contact-state replay and common clock, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Loss-of-contact duration fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「離線時間比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定辨識門檻的合成時窗如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間造成偏離的合成觀察，以離線起迄時間與事件數說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Loss-of-contact duration fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Synthetic window with a fixed detection definition. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations. Explain which evidence in contact-loss start/end times and event count distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以離線起迄時間與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用接觸狀態重播與共同時鐘建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「離線時間比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use contact-loss start/end times and event count to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using contact-state replay and common clock, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Loss-of-contact duration fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「離線時間比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定辨識門檻的合成時窗如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間造成偏離的合成觀察，以離線起迄時間與事件數說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Loss-of-contact duration fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Synthetic window with a fixed detection definition. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations. Explain which evidence in contact-loss start/end times and event count distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「離線時間比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Loss-of-contact duration fraction\"?","options":["本單元以離線起迄時間與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用接觸狀態重播與共同時鐘建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段"],"optionsEn":["Use contact-loss start/end times and event count to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以離線起迄時間與事件數區分模型與觀察，先用接觸狀態重播與共同時鐘建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use contact-loss start/end times and event count to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b361-v16-16","title":"離線時間比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Loss-of-contact duration fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「離線時間比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Loss-of-contact duration fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間。這個失效與「離線時間比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查離線起迄時間與事件數，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations. This failure and a measurement bias in Loss-of-contact duration fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check contact-loss start/end times and event count rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用離線起迄時間與事件數作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間。這個失效與「離線時間比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查離線起迄時間與事件數，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations. This failure and a measurement bias in Loss-of-contact duration fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check contact-loss start/end times and event count rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「離線時間比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Loss-of-contact duration fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: External flashes may create false arc detections."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b361-v16-s3","title":"電弧事件時間與接觸點抬升量","titleEn":"Arc-event exposure fraction & Contact-point uplift scale","description":"本階段聚焦「電弧事件時間」與「接觸點抬升量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Arc-event exposure fraction\" and \"Contact-point uplift scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b361-v16-17","title":"電弧事件時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Arc-event exposure fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「電弧事件時間」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Arc-event exposure fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"電弧時間需定義偵測頻寬與事件合併規則。本模型把 arc 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.044 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。僅用既有合成事件，不產生真實電弧。使用光學事件與電流同步作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「電弧事件時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Arc duration requires defined sensing bandwidth and event-merging rules. In this model, arc is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.044 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Use synthetic recorded events only, without creating real arcs. Use optical events synchronized with current as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. External flashes may create false arc detections; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Arc-event exposure fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：arc=12 ms, test=30 s；y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: arc=12 ms, test=30 s; y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: External flashes may create false arc detections.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「電弧事件時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Arc-event exposure fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-17-k1","title":"電弧事件時間","titleEn":"Arc-event exposure fraction","text":"電弧時間需定義偵測頻寬與事件合併規則。本模型把 arc 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.044 percent。","textEn":"Arc duration requires defined sensing bandwidth and event-merging rules. In this model, arc is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: External flashes may create false arc detections. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電弧事件時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Arc-event exposure fraction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升","電弧時間需定義偵測頻寬與事件合併規則。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: External flashes may create false arc detections.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift.","Arc duration requires defined sensing bandwidth and event-merging rules."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電弧時間需定義偵測頻寬與事件合併規則。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Arc duration requires defined sensing bandwidth and event-merging rules. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b361-v16-18","title":"電弧事件時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Arc-event exposure fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「電弧事件時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Arc-event exposure fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：arc=12 ms, test=30 s；y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent。只把 arc 增加百分之十，y=0.044 percent。模型邊界：僅用既有合成事件，不產生真實電弧；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: arc=12 ms, test=30 s; y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent. Increasing only arc with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.044 percent. Boundary: Use synthetic recorded events only, without creating real arcs; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以光學事件與電流同步區分模型與觀察，先用合成光電訊號與時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use optical events synchronized with current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：arc=12 ms, test=30 s；y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent。只把 arc 增加百分之十，y=0.044 percent。模型邊界：僅用既有合成事件，不產生真實電弧；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: arc=12 ms, test=30 s; y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent. Increasing only arc with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.044 percent. Boundary: Use synthetic recorded events only, without creating real arcs; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電弧事件時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Arc-event exposure fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：arc=12 ms, test=30 s；y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: arc=12 ms, test=30 s; y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：arc=12 ms, test=30 s；y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: arc=12 ms, test=30 s; y=arc/(test*1000)*100=0.04 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b361-v16-19","title":"電弧事件時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Arc-event exposure fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「電弧事件時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Arc-event exposure fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以光學事件與電流同步區分模型與觀察，先用合成光電訊號與時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「電弧事件時間」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use optical events synchronized with current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic optical/electrical signals and timestamps, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Arc-event exposure fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「電弧事件時間」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出僅用既有合成事件，不產生真實電弧如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件造成偏離的合成觀察，以光學事件與電流同步說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Arc-event exposure fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Use synthetic recorded events only, without creating real arcs. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: External flashes may create false arc detections. Explain which evidence in optical events synchronized with current distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: External flashes may create false arc detections. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以光學事件與電流同步區分模型與觀察，先用合成光電訊號與時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「電弧事件時間」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use optical events synchronized with current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic optical/electrical signals and timestamps, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Arc-event exposure fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「電弧事件時間」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出僅用既有合成事件，不產生真實電弧如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件造成偏離的合成觀察，以光學事件與電流同步說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Arc-event exposure fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Use synthetic recorded events only, without creating real arcs. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: External flashes may create false arc detections. Explain which evidence in optical events synchronized with current distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電弧事件時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Arc-event exposure fraction\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以光學事件與電流同步區分模型與觀察，先用合成光電訊號與時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use optical events synchronized with current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以光學事件與電流同步區分模型與觀察，先用合成光電訊號與時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use optical events synchronized with current to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b361-v16-20","title":"電弧事件時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Arc-event exposure fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「電弧事件時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Arc-event exposure fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件。這個失效與「電弧事件時間」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查光學事件與電流同步，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"External flashes may create false arc detections. This failure and a measurement bias in Arc-event exposure fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check optical events synchronized with current rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用光學事件與電流同步作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: External flashes may create false arc detections; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: External flashes may create false arc detections.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件。這個失效與「電弧事件時間」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查光學事件與電流同步，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"External flashes may create false arc detections. This failure and a measurement bias in Arc-event exposure fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check optical events synchronized with current rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電弧事件時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Arc-event exposure fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升","外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift.","External flashes may create false arc detections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"External flashes may create false arc detections. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b361-v16-21","title":"接觸點抬升量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Contact-point uplift scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「接觸點抬升量」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Contact-point uplift scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"線性等效剛度把接觸力連到局部抬升。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 9.16667 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。指定接觸位置的靜態等效剛度。使用接觸點與支點位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接觸點抬升量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Linear equivalent stiffness links contact force to local uplift. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 9.16667 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Static equivalent stiffness at a specified contact position. Use contact and support displacements as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Contact-point uplift scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=12000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=12000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接觸點抬升量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Contact-point uplift scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-21-k1","title":"接觸點抬升量","titleEn":"Contact-point uplift scale","text":"線性等效剛度把接觸力連到局部抬升。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 9.16667 mm。","textEn":"Linear equivalent stiffness links contact force to local uplift. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸點抬升量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Contact-point uplift scale\" is correct?","options":["線性等效剛度把接觸力連到局部抬升。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差"],"optionsEn":["Linear equivalent stiffness links contact force to local uplift.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"線性等效剛度把接觸力連到局部抬升。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Linear equivalent stiffness links contact force to local uplift. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b361-v16-22","title":"接觸點抬升量：定量估算","titleEn":"Contact-point uplift scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接觸點抬升量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Contact-point uplift scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=12000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=9.16667 mm。模型邊界：指定接觸位置的靜態等效剛度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=12000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=9.16667 mm. Boundary: Static equivalent stiffness at a specified contact position; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以接觸點與支點位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載弦模型與雷射位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use contact and support displacements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=12000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=9.16667 mm。模型邊界：指定接觸位置的靜態等效剛度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=12000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=9.16667 mm. Boundary: Static equivalent stiffness at a specified contact position; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接觸點抬升量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Contact-point uplift scale\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=12000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=12000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=12000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=12000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=8.33333 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b361-v16-23","title":"接觸點抬升量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Contact-point uplift scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接觸點抬升量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Contact-point uplift scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以接觸點與支點位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載弦模型與雷射位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接觸點抬升量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use contact and support displacements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load string model and laser displacement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Contact-point uplift scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「接觸點抬升量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出指定接觸位置的靜態等效剛度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升造成偏離的合成觀察，以接觸點與支點位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Contact-point uplift scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Static equivalent stiffness at a specified contact position. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift. Explain which evidence in contact and support displacements distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以接觸點與支點位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載弦模型與雷射位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接觸點抬升量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use contact and support displacements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load string model and laser displacement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Contact-point uplift scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「接觸點抬升量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出指定接觸位置的靜態等效剛度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升造成偏離的合成觀察，以接觸點與支點位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Contact-point uplift scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Static equivalent stiffness at a specified contact position. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift. Explain which evidence in contact and support displacements distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接觸點抬升量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Contact-point uplift scale\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布","本單元以接觸點與支點位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載弦模型與雷射位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread.","Use contact and support displacements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以接觸點與支點位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載弦模型與雷射位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use contact and support displacements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b361-v16-24","title":"接觸點抬升量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Contact-point uplift scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接觸點抬升量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Contact-point uplift scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升。這個失效與「接觸點抬升量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接觸點與支點位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift. This failure and a measurement bias in Contact-point uplift scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check contact and support displacements rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用接觸點與支點位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升。這個失效與「接觸點抬升量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接觸點與支點位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift. This failure and a measurement bias in Contact-point uplift scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check contact and support displacements rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接觸點抬升量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Contact-point uplift scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差"],"optionsEn":["Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b361-v16-s4","title":"弓頭慣性修正與測試訊號取樣","titleEn":"Pantograph-head inertia correction & Test-signal sample interval","description":"本階段聚焦「弓頭慣性修正」與「測試訊號取樣」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pantograph-head inertia correction\" and \"Test-signal sample interval\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b361-v16-25","title":"弓頭慣性修正：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pantograph-head inertia correction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「弓頭慣性修正」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pantograph-head inertia correction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"加速度造成慣性項，感測器內力不一定直接等於接觸力。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 17.6 N。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。剛性弓頭的一維平動。使用加速度與力的共同相位作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「弓頭慣性修正」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Acceleration produces an inertia term, so measured internal force may differ from contact force. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 17.6 N. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. One-dimensional rigid-head translation. Use common phase of acceleration and force as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pantograph-head inertia correction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2；y=m*a=16 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2; y=m*a=16 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「弓頭慣性修正」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pantograph-head inertia correction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-25-k1","title":"弓頭慣性修正","titleEn":"Pantograph-head inertia correction","text":"加速度造成慣性項，感測器內力不一定直接等於接觸力。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 17.6 N。","textEn":"Acceleration produces an inertia term, so measured internal force may differ from contact force. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「弓頭慣性修正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pantograph-head inertia correction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差","加速度造成慣性項，感測器內力不一定直接等於接觸力。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias.","Acceleration produces an inertia term, so measured internal force may differ from contact force.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies."],"answer":1,"explanation":"加速度造成慣性項，感測器內力不一定直接等於接觸力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Acceleration produces an inertia term, so measured internal force may differ from contact force. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b361-v16-26","title":"弓頭慣性修正：定量估算","titleEn":"Pantograph-head inertia correction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「弓頭慣性修正」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pantograph-head inertia correction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2；y=m*a=16 N。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=17.6 N。模型邊界：剛性弓頭的一維平動；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2; y=m*a=16 N. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=17.6 N. Boundary: One-dimensional rigid-head translation; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以加速度與力的共同相位區分模型與觀察，先用模型力計與加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use common phase of acceleration and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2；y=m*a=16 N。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=17.6 N。模型邊界：剛性弓頭的一維平動；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2; y=m*a=16 N. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=17.6 N. Boundary: One-dimensional rigid-head translation; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「弓頭慣性修正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pantograph-head inertia correction\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2；y=m*a=16 N。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2; y=m*a=16 N."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2；y=m*a=16 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=8 kg, a=2 m/s2; y=m*a=16 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b361-v16-27","title":"弓頭慣性修正：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pantograph-head inertia correction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「弓頭慣性修正」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pantograph-head inertia correction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以加速度與力的共同相位區分模型與觀察，先用模型力計與加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「弓頭慣性修正」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use common phase of acceleration and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model force gauge and accelerometer, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Pantograph-head inertia correction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「弓頭慣性修正」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出剛性弓頭的一維平動如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差造成偏離的合成觀察，以加速度與力的共同相位說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Pantograph-head inertia correction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One-dimensional rigid-head translation. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias. Explain which evidence in common phase of acceleration and force distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以加速度與力的共同相位區分模型與觀察，先用模型力計與加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「弓頭慣性修正」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use common phase of acceleration and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model force gauge and accelerometer, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Pantograph-head inertia correction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「弓頭慣性修正」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出剛性弓頭的一維平動如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差造成偏離的合成觀察，以加速度與力的共同相位說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Pantograph-head inertia correction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One-dimensional rigid-head translation. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias. Explain which evidence in common phase of acceleration and force distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「弓頭慣性修正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pantograph-head inertia correction\"?","options":["本單元以加速度與力的共同相位區分模型與觀察，先用模型力計與加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間"],"optionsEn":["Use common phase of acceleration and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以加速度與力的共同相位區分模型與觀察，先用模型力計與加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use common phase of acceleration and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b361-v16-28","title":"弓頭慣性修正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pantograph-head inertia correction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「弓頭慣性修正」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pantograph-head inertia correction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差。這個失效與「弓頭慣性修正」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查加速度與力的共同相位，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias. This failure and a measurement bias in Pantograph-head inertia correction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check common phase of acceleration and force rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用加速度與力的共同相位作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差。這個失效與「弓頭慣性修正」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查加速度與力的共同相位，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias. This failure and a measurement bias in Pantograph-head inertia correction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check common phase of acceleration and force rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「弓頭慣性修正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pantograph-head inertia correction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies."],"answer":1,"explanation":"質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b361-v16-29","title":"測試訊號取樣：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Test-signal sample interval: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「測試訊號取樣」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Test-signal sample interval” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"取樣間隔決定離散時間點但不能替代抗混疊濾波。本模型把 fs 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出減少為 0.454545 ms。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均勻取樣且時鐘穩定。使用原始頻寬與取樣設定作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測試訊號取樣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sample interval defines discrete timing but does not replace anti-alias filtering. In this model, fs is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output decreases to 0.454545 ms. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform sampling with a stable clock. Use original bandwidth and sampling settings as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Test-signal sample interval” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：fs=2000 Hz；y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: fs=2000 Hz; y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測試訊號取樣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Test-signal sample interval”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-29-k1","title":"測試訊號取樣","titleEn":"Test-signal sample interval","text":"取樣間隔決定離散時間點但不能替代抗混疊濾波。本模型把 fs 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出減少為 0.454545 ms。","textEn":"Sample interval defines discrete timing but does not replace anti-alias filtering. In this model, fs is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測試訊號取樣」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Test-signal sample interval\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點","取樣間隔決定離散時間點但不能替代抗混疊濾波。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper.","Sample interval defines discrete timing but does not replace anti-alias filtering."],"answer":2,"explanation":"取樣間隔決定離散時間點但不能替代抗混疊濾波。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sample interval defines discrete timing but does not replace anti-alias filtering. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b361-v16-30","title":"測試訊號取樣：定量估算","titleEn":"Test-signal sample interval: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測試訊號取樣」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Test-signal sample interval” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：fs=2000 Hz；y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms。只把 fs 增加百分之十，y=0.454545 ms。模型邊界：均勻取樣且時鐘穩定；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: fs=2000 Hz; y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms. Increasing only fs with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.454545 ms. Boundary: Uniform sampling with a stable clock; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以原始頻寬與取樣設定區分模型與觀察，先用合成掃頻與濾波紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use original bandwidth and sampling settings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：fs=2000 Hz；y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms。只把 fs 增加百分之十，y=0.454545 ms。模型邊界：均勻取樣且時鐘穩定；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: fs=2000 Hz; y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms. Increasing only fs with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.454545 ms. Boundary: Uniform sampling with a stable clock; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測試訊號取樣」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Test-signal sample interval\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：fs=2000 Hz；y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: fs=2000 Hz; y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：fs=2000 Hz；y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: fs=2000 Hz; y=1/fs*1000=0.5 ms. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b361-v16-31","title":"測試訊號取樣：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Test-signal sample interval: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測試訊號取樣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Test-signal sample interval” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以原始頻寬與取樣設定區分模型與觀察，先用合成掃頻與濾波紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「測試訊號取樣」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use original bandwidth and sampling settings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic frequency sweep and filter records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Test-signal sample interval. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「測試訊號取樣」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻取樣且時鐘穩定如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動造成偏離的合成觀察，以原始頻寬與取樣設定說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Test-signal sample interval, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform sampling with a stable clock. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies. Explain which evidence in original bandwidth and sampling settings distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以原始頻寬與取樣設定區分模型與觀察，先用合成掃頻與濾波紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「測試訊號取樣」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use original bandwidth and sampling settings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic frequency sweep and filter records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Test-signal sample interval. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「測試訊號取樣」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻取樣且時鐘穩定如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動造成偏離的合成觀察，以原始頻寬與取樣設定說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Test-signal sample interval, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform sampling with a stable clock. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies. Explain which evidence in original bandwidth and sampling settings distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測試訊號取樣」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Test-signal sample interval\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以原始頻寬與取樣設定區分模型與觀察，先用合成掃頻與濾波紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use original bandwidth and sampling settings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: External flashes may create false arc detections."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以原始頻寬與取樣設定區分模型與觀察，先用合成掃頻與濾波紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use original bandwidth and sampling settings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b361-v16-32","title":"測試訊號取樣：失效診斷","titleEn":"Test-signal sample interval: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測試訊號取樣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Test-signal sample interval” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動。這個失效與「測試訊號取樣」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查原始頻寬與取樣設定，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies. This failure and a measurement bias in Test-signal sample interval can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check original bandwidth and sampling settings rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用原始頻寬與取樣設定作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動。這個失效與「測試訊號取樣」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查原始頻寬與取樣設定，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies. This failure and a measurement bias in Test-signal sample interval can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check original bandwidth and sampling settings rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測試訊號取樣」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Test-signal sample interval\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點","超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper.","Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"超頻成分折返會產生假低頻振動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Out-of-band content aliases into false low frequencies. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b361-v16-s5","title":"感測延遲位置偏移與合成量測不確定度","titleEn":"Sensor-delay spatial offset & Combined force uncertainty","description":"本階段聚焦「感測延遲位置偏移」與「合成量測不確定度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sensor-delay spatial offset\" and \"Combined force uncertainty\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b361-v16-33","title":"感測延遲位置偏移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sensor-delay spatial offset: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「感測延遲位置偏移」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sensor-delay spatial offset” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"時延經車速轉換為里程錯位。本模型把 v 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.352 m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。延遲期間等速。使用訊號對時與里程標記作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「感測延遲位置偏移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Time delay becomes chainage error through train speed. In this model, v is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.352 m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Constant speed during the delay. Use signal synchronization and chainage markers as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sensor-delay spatial offset” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s；y=v*delay=0.32 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s; y=v*delay=0.32 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「感測延遲位置偏移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sensor-delay spatial offset”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-33-k1","title":"感測延遲位置偏移","titleEn":"Sensor-delay spatial offset","text":"時延經車速轉換為里程錯位。本模型把 v 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.352 m。","textEn":"Time delay becomes chainage error through train speed. In this model, v is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「感測延遲位置偏移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sensor-delay spatial offset\" is correct?","options":["時延經車速轉換為里程錯位。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度"],"optionsEn":["Time delay becomes chainage error through train speed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty."],"answer":0,"explanation":"時延經車速轉換為里程錯位。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Time delay becomes chainage error through train speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b361-v16-34","title":"感測延遲位置偏移：定量估算","titleEn":"Sensor-delay spatial offset: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「感測延遲位置偏移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sensor-delay spatial offset” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s；y=v*delay=0.32 m。只把 v 增加百分之十，y=0.352 m。模型邊界：延遲期間等速；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s; y=v*delay=0.32 m. Increasing only v with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.352 m. Boundary: Constant speed during the delay; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以訊號對時與里程標記區分模型與觀察，先用共同脈衝與里程資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use signal synchronization and chainage markers to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s；y=v*delay=0.32 m。只把 v 增加百分之十，y=0.352 m。模型邊界：延遲期間等速；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s; y=v*delay=0.32 m. Increasing only v with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.352 m. Boundary: Constant speed during the delay; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「感測延遲位置偏移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sensor-delay spatial offset\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：少數尖峰可提高均方根卻被平均掩蓋","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s；y=v*delay=0.32 m。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：相同事件數可能有完全不同中斷時間"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A few peaks raise RMS while a mean hides them.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s; y=v*delay=0.32 m.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Equal event counts can conceal very different interruption durations."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s；y=v*delay=0.32 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, delay=0.004 s; y=v*delay=0.32 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b361-v16-35","title":"感測延遲位置偏移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sensor-delay spatial offset: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「感測延遲位置偏移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sensor-delay spatial offset” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以訊號對時與里程標記區分模型與觀察，先用共同脈衝與里程資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「感測延遲位置偏移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use signal synchronization and chainage markers to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using common timing pulse and chainage data, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Sensor-delay spatial offset. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「感測延遲位置偏移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出延遲期間等速如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點造成偏離的合成觀察，以訊號對時與里程標記說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Sensor-delay spatial offset, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant speed during the delay. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper. Explain which evidence in signal synchronization and chainage markers distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以訊號對時與里程標記區分模型與觀察，先用共同脈衝與里程資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「感測延遲位置偏移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use signal synchronization and chainage markers to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using common timing pulse and chainage data, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Sensor-delay spatial offset. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「感測延遲位置偏移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出延遲期間等速如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點造成偏離的合成觀察，以訊號對時與里程標記說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Sensor-delay spatial offset, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant speed during the delay. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper. Explain which evidence in signal synchronization and chainage markers distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「感測延遲位置偏移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sensor-delay spatial offset\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把跨中剛度套到吊點會錯估抬升","本單元以訊號對時與里程標記區分模型與觀察，先用共同脈衝與里程資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using midspan stiffness at a dropper misestimates uplift.","Use signal synchronization and chainage markers to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以訊號對時與里程標記區分模型與觀察，先用共同脈衝與里程資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use signal synchronization and chainage markers to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b361-v16-36","title":"感測延遲位置偏移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sensor-delay spatial offset: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「感測延遲位置偏移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sensor-delay spatial offset” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點。這個失效與「感測延遲位置偏移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查訊號對時與里程標記，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper. This failure and a measurement bias in Sensor-delay spatial offset can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check signal synchronization and chainage markers rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用訊號對時與里程標記作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點。這個失效與「感測延遲位置偏移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查訊號對時與里程標記，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper. This failure and a measurement bias in Sensor-delay spatial offset can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check signal synchronization and chainage markers rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「感測延遲位置偏移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sensor-delay spatial offset\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度"],"optionsEn":["Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未校正時延會把缺陷定位到錯誤吊點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uncorrected delay assigns a defect to the wrong dropper. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b361-v16-37","title":"合成量測不確定度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Combined force uncertainty: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「合成量測不確定度」如何影響高速鐵路受流性能驗證的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Combined force uncertainty” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Current-collection verification for high-speed rail”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"獨立標準不確定度可平方和合成，相關項須加共變異。本模型把 sensor 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.85227 N。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。零共變異的一階近似。使用各項校正與相關性作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「合成量測不確定度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Independent standard uncertainties combine by root-sum-square; correlated terms require covariance. In this model, sensor is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 3.85227 N. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. First-order approximation with zero covariance. Use calibration and correlation of each contribution as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Combined force uncertainty” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N；y=sqrt(sensor**2+inertia**2+sync**2)=3.74166 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N; y=sqrt(sensor**2+inertia**2+sync**2)=3.74166 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「合成量測不確定度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Combined force uncertainty”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-37-k1","title":"合成量測不確定度","titleEn":"Combined force uncertainty","text":"獨立標準不確定度可平方和合成，相關項須加共變異。本模型把 sensor 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.85227 N。","textEn":"Independent standard uncertainties combine by root-sum-square; correlated terms require covariance. In this model, sensor is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「合成量測不確定度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Combined force uncertainty\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度","獨立標準不確定度可平方和合成，相關項須加共變異。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty.","Independent standard uncertainties combine by root-sum-square; correlated terms require covariance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals."],"answer":1,"explanation":"獨立標準不確定度可平方和合成，相關項須加共變異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Independent standard uncertainties combine by root-sum-square; correlated terms require covariance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b361-v16-38","title":"合成量測不確定度：定量估算","titleEn":"Combined force uncertainty: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「合成量測不確定度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Combined force uncertainty” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N；y=sqrt(sensor**2+inertia**2+sync**2)=3.74166 N。只把 sensor 增加百分之十，y=3.85227 N。模型邊界：零共變異的一階近似；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N; y=sqrt(sensor**2+inertia**2+sync**2)=3.74166 N. Increasing only sensor with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.85227 N. Boundary: First-order approximation with zero covariance; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以各項校正與相關性區分模型與觀察，先用校正證據與重複測試建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use calibration and correlation of each contribution to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N；y=sqrt(sensor**2+inertia**2+sync**2)=3.74166 N。只把 sensor 增加百分之十，y=3.85227 N。模型邊界：零共變異的一階近似；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N; y=sqrt(sensor**2+inertia**2+sync**2)=3.74166 N. Increasing only sensor with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.85227 N. Boundary: First-order approximation with zero covariance; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「合成量測不確定度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Combined force uncertainty\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：混合不同速度時窗會把工況差當隨機散布","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外界閃光可能造成假電弧事件","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing speed regimes confuses operating changes with random spread.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: External flashes may create false arc detections.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N; y=sqrt(sensor**2+inertia**2+sync**2)=3.74166 N."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N；y=sqrt(sensor**2+inertia**2+sync**2)=3.74166 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: sensor=2 N, inertia=3 N, sync=1 N; y=sqrt(sensor**2+inertia**2+sync**2)=3.74166 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b361-v16-39","title":"合成量測不確定度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Combined force uncertainty: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「合成量測不確定度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Combined force uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以各項校正與相關性區分模型與觀察，先用校正證據與重複測試建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「合成量測不確定度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use calibration and correlation of each contribution to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using calibration evidence and repeat tests, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Combined force uncertainty. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「合成量測不確定度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出零共變異的一階近似如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度造成偏離的合成觀察，以各項校正與相關性說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Combined force uncertainty, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: First-order approximation with zero covariance. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty. Explain which evidence in calibration and correlation of each contribution distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以各項校正與相關性區分模型與觀察，先用校正證據與重複測試建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「合成量測不確定度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use calibration and correlation of each contribution to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using calibration evidence and repeat tests, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Combined force uncertainty. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「合成量測不確定度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出零共變異的一階近似如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度造成偏離的合成觀察，以各項校正與相關性說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Combined force uncertainty, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: First-order approximation with zero covariance. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty. Explain which evidence in calibration and correlation of each contribution distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「合成量測不確定度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Combined force uncertainty\"?","options":["本單元以各項校正與相關性區分模型與觀察，先用校正證據與重複測試建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：質量或加速度正負號錯誤會加倍偏差"],"optionsEn":["Use calibration and correlation of each contribution to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wrong mass or acceleration sign can increase bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以各項校正與相關性區分模型與觀察，先用校正證據與重複測試建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use calibration and correlation of each contribution to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b361-v16-40","title":"合成量測不確定度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Combined force uncertainty: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b361-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「合成量測不確定度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Combined force uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度。這個失效與「合成量測不確定度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各項校正與相關性，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty. This failure and a measurement bias in Combined force uncertainty can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check calibration and correlation of each contribution rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用各項校正與相關性作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b361-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度。這個失效與「合成量測不確定度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各項校正與相關性，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty. This failure and a measurement bias in Combined force uncertainty can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check calibration and correlation of each contribution rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b361-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「合成量測不確定度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Combined force uncertainty\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：正常平均可同時含零接觸片段"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A normal mean can include zero-contact intervals."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把共同偏差當獨立會低估力不確定度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating shared bias as independent understates uncertainty. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b361-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b361-en.svg"}};
